  <iati-identifier>CH-FDJP-110.162.567-FIND2023</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="CH-FDJP-110.162.567" type="30">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Foundation for Innovative New Diagnostics</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensure equitable access to reliable diagnosis around the world</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FIND&#x2019;s focus as a PDP remains on fostering innovation, product development and evidence generation for diagnostics. To maximize the impact of these technical activities, FIND has sustained advocacy efforts on 
testing and global policy engagement while expanding engagement with countries to ensure that the 
diagnostics R&amp;D agenda is responsive to country needs.

In the context of our R&amp;D portfolio, as COVID-19-related activities were being brought to fruition in 2023, we 
gradually fostered a shift towards supporting product advances that can be leveraged to impact other diseases and syndromes. In particular, novel molecular point-of-care (POC) multiplex testing platforms developed for COVID-19, and with the potential to offer the accuracy of molecular testing in decentralized settings, such as primary healthcare clinics, at affordable prices, were expanded to include a broader test menu across a range of diseases. These products now comprise a considerable proportion of our pipeline, along with disease-specific rapid diagnostic tests (RDTs) and non-diagnostic products such as digital tools. Our robust portfolio 
continues to have an impact, including in primary healthcare settings.</narrative>
  </description>
